.TH PROJECTHUB 1 "November 2026" "ProjectHub 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
projecthub \- manage and open development projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B projecthub
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ProjectHub
is a desktop application that keeps a list of local project directories and
opens them in a code editor (Zed or Sublime Text), a terminal (Ghostty or a
configured terminal) or the file manager.
It shows the Git branch and uncommitted changes of each project and offers a
system tray menu with recently opened projects.
.PP
Only one instance runs per desktop session.
Starting
.B projecthub
again brings the running window to the front.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/projecthub/settings.json
User preferences (default
.IR ~/.config/projecthub/settings.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/projecthub/projects.json
The project catalog.
Replacement imports keep a backup next to it as
.IR projects.json.bak\-<timestamp> .
.PP
Both files are created on first use and are not removed when the package is
uninstalled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1)
.PP
https://github.com/semelyanov86/ProjectHub
